.TH MAGUS-NOTIFY 1 "" "magus" "magus Manual"
.SH NAME
magus\-notify \- Normalize an attention event and optionally notify the local desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magus
.RI "notify [\-\-outcome <vocab>] [\-\-desktop]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Raise one canonical attention event.
.PP
The input is read from stdin and may be plain text or a complete event JSON
envelope. Either way the result is one normalized event, so a caller that
knows nothing about magus's event schema can still raise a well\-formed one.
.PP
\-\-outcome names the event's outcome vocabulary. \-\-desktop additionally
raises an operating\-system notification, which is the part a human notices;
without it the event is recorded and nothing pops up.
.SH OPTIONS
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-desktop\fR
Also raise an OS notification
.TP
\fB\-\-outcome\fR \fIstring\fR
Outcome vocabulary for the event
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
\fIRaise a permission prompt on the desktop\fR
.PP
.EX
printf '%s\(rsn' 'needs approval' | magus notify --outcome permission --desktop
.EE
.PP
\fIRaise a pre\-built event envelope\fR
.PP
.EX
printf '%s\(rsn' '{"outcome":"permission","source":{"kind":"agent"},"message":"needs approval"}' | magus notify --desktop
.EE
.PP
